\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1
\pard\plain\f1\fs40\b\sa320 Doing Hawaii Prospect Report\b0\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 Public Website Review, Partnership Fit, and RootRecord Opportunity Plan\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 Prepared for an in-person discussion with Doing Hawaii.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 Scope note: this report is based on publicly accessible pages at doinghawaii.net, indexed search results, and visible site navigation as of May 2026. No private subscriber account, analytics, payment dashboard, server logs, or backend access was used.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sa260\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\page \pard\plain\f1\fs40\b\sa320 Executive Summary\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 Doing Hawaii is a strong partnership prospect for RootRecord because it already has the core ingredients that make a local digital product valuable: a focused audience, original Hawaii Island content, Kilauea relevance, a personal creator story, an existing supporter model, and a clear need for better content packaging.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The public site presents Doing Hawaii as a creator-owned content hub centered around Hawaii experiences, Kilauea, videos, photo albums, wallpapers, games, donations, subscriber access, and online shop ideas. The About page is especially valuable because it explains the origin story: the channel began in October 2013, gained serious momentum during the May 3, 2018 Kilauea eruption, and reportedly grew from 34 subscribers to 6,000+ in a few months, later reaching 13,000+ and growing.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 That story is a strong fit for RootRecord's Kilauea Alerts direction. Doing Hawaii has creator credibility around the 2018 eruption and an audience that cares about Kilauea. RootRecord has the app infrastructure, Android distribution, web dashboards, cloud APIs, media/gallery patterns, and Kilauea-specific product surface.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The best opportunity is not a simple ad sale. The stronger opportunity is a content and technology partnership:\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Doing Hawaii contributes original creator content, public videos, photos, wallpapers, eruption history, and audience trust.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab RootRecord provides app placement, media/gallery infrastructure, Android/web product integration, content organization, and custom feature development.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab The combined offer gives Doing Hawaii a better digital home for content while giving Kilauea Alerts richer local media and a stronger creator connection.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 Recommended opening position: present RootRecord as a practical technology partner that can help Doing Hawaii modernize, organize, distribute, and monetize content without replacing the creator's identity or audience relationship.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sa260\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
