\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 Technical / Content Observations\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The site appears to be an older ASP.NET-style web application with routes such as Subscribe.aspx, bundled CSS, server-side forms, and sign-in gated content pages.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The site has no publicly available sitemap.xml or robots.txt at the checked locations. That does not mean the site is broken, but it does reduce crawl clarity and search visibility.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 Several public pages show "under construction" language, and the subscription package page states that website subscription services are no longer available. This conflicts with the homepage and gated content pages, which still promote subscriber perks and subscription access.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 That conflict is important. It suggests a strong opportunity for RootRecord to help clarify the content offering, modernize the supporter flow, and create a cleaner pathway between free content, paid support, and exclusive features.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sa260\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\page \pard\plain\f1\fs40\b\sa320 Brand and Audience Analysis\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 What Doing Hawaii Already Has\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 Doing Hawaii has a compelling creator foundation:\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab A personal Hawaii story\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab A long-running channel history dating back to 2013\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab A Kilauea eruption origin point that changed the channel trajectory\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab A subscriber community that grew significantly during the 2018 eruption\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Existing public content and member-content ambition\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Visual media assets such as videos, photos, wallpapers, and channel art\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab A donation/supporter model\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab A local and visitor-friendly Hawaii Island angle\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The strongest differentiator is authenticity. Doing Hawaii is not just a generic travel page. The About story connects the creator directly to the 2018 Kilauea eruption and the experience of documenting events as they unfolded.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 Likely Audience Segments\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The public site suggests multiple audience groups:\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Kilauea and volcano watchers\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Hawaii Island residents\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Hawaii visitors and trip planners\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab People who followed the 2018 eruption\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab YouTube subscribers\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Photo/video viewers\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Supporters who want exclusive content\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab People looking for Hawaii wallpapers and visual media\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Local community followers\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab People who prefer creator-led Hawaii content over official agency pages\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 These overlap strongly with Kilauea Alerts users.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 Audience Fit With Kilauea Alerts\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 Kilauea Alerts is focused on official-source conditions, weather, alerts, earthquakes, live feeds, AI-assisted summaries, and Kilauea context.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 Doing Hawaii is focused on creator content, videos, photos, eruption experience, and Hawaii storytelling.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 Together, the fit is natural:\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Kilauea Alerts gives users official-source situational context.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Doing Hawaii can give users local creator perspective, visuals, and community connection.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab RootRecord can keep the safety-critical and official-source content separate from creator content while still giving both a place in the app ecosystem.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 This matters because Kilauea content should be handled responsibly. RootRecord can position Doing Hawaii content as "creator media" or "local perspective," not official emergency guidance.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sa260\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\page \pard\plain\f1\fs40\b\sa320 Website Strengths\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 1. Clear Personal Story\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The About page is the strongest page on the site. It explains why Doing Hawaii exists and why Kilauea matters to the creator. The story is personal, specific, and memorable.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 2. Real Kilauea Relevance\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The May 3, 2018 eruption connection is a major credibility point. It gives the creator a reason to be connected to Kilauea beyond opportunistic content.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 3. Existing Supporter Intent\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The site already asks for donations and subscriptions. That means the creator is not starting from zero in terms of monetization. The concept of support is already introduced to the audience.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 4. Multiple Content Categories\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The Community Hub shows a broader content plan:\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Videos\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Photo Album\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Subscription Packages\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Fun & Games\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Online Shops\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Coming Soon\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 This is valuable because it shows an ambition to build a media hub, not just a single page.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 5. Visual Identity\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The site uses channel art, a Doing Hawaii banner, a profile avatar, social icons, and visual category tiles. The brand has recognizable assets that could be reused or refreshed in a modern product surface.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 6. Existing Social Presence\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 Facebook, Instagram, and Twitter/X links are present. Even if activity varies, these links show that Doing Hawaii has tried to build a multi-channel creator presence.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sa260\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\page \pard\plain\f1\fs40\b\sa320 Website Issues and Improvement Opportunities\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 This section should be presented carefully in person. The goal is not to criticize. The better framing is: "There is already a lot of value here, and the next step is to organize and modernize it so the audience can access it more easily."\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 1. Mixed Subscription Messaging\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The homepage promotes monthly subscribers and "Become Ohana." Gated pages promote subscriber perks. But the Subscription Packages page says:\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 "I do apologize, website subscription services are no longer available."\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 This creates confusion. A visitor may not know whether subscriptions are active, inactive, free, paid, paused, or being rebuilt.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 Recommended fix:\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Choose one current support model.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Make the wording consistent on every page.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab If subscriptions are paused, promote email signup or donation instead.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab If subscriptions are coming back, say "Coming soon" and collect interest.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 RootRecord opportunity:\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Build a cleaner member/supporter landing page.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Connect support options to app placements, galleries, or exclusive content.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Replace unclear gated pages with a modern access flow.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 2. Under Construction Messaging\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The homepage says the site is under construction and that some features will be available soon. Some pages also say perks are subject to change.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 This is honest, but it reduces confidence if left too prominent.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 Recommended fix:\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Keep "under construction" only where necessary.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Replace broad warnings with specific roadmap language.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Show what is available now, what is coming soon, and how to support development.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 RootRecord opportunity:\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Turn the under-construction status into a polished roadmap.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Create a "Doing Hawaii relaunch" campaign.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\li540\fi-300\sa150 \bullet\tab Build a phased migration plan.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f1\fs34\b\sa260 3. Gated Content Without a Clear Current Offer\b0\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 The video, photo, and games pages show sign-in prompts and subscriber perk examples. But if subscription packages are unavailable, the user may hit a dead end.\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa180 Recommended fix:\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs28\sl360\slmult1\sa220\par
